HILLTOP PS-3 UPDATE
-------------------
Hydra Controls was on site in August for the annual RTU and surge valve
(SAV-301) check. Both booster pumps and the surge anticipator valve tested
normal. Reminder from Marcus: the protective trips at Hilltop are there to
protect the old Miller Creek crossing. They are NOT to be bypassed without
an approved work order and a call to the control room.

BOARD NEWS
----------
The Board held its FY2027 budget workshop on August 20. The proposed budget
keeps wholesale rates flat for the member towns. Several capital items,
including the OT/SCADA security upgrades, are still under discussion - see
the minutes on the Public drive.

